From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:23:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/30] gpu_display + main: iceland gvm: --vnc-server, a
 headless VNC display (LibVNCServer bridge ported from DroidVM)

crosvm run --vnc-server [host=ADDR][,port=N][,password-file=PATH] (feature vnc, links libvncserver):
- gpu_display/src/vnc_server_bridge.c/.h, vnc_frame_consumer.h: DroidVM dvm-crosvm 849e05f (GPL-2.0-or-later +
  ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS, header kept) without the H.264 path: honest listener binding, keysym map, input ring,
  32-row damage bands, cursor compositing over a clean frame
- gpu_display/src/gpu_display_vnc.rs: DisplayVnc reduced to the CPU transport (the copy path / simplefb bridge
  write the surface, flip offers it), cursor surface, RFB pointer -> Tablet events in guest pixels (buttons,
  wheel, hwheel), keys -> Keyboard events; GVM-VNC listening / GVM-VNC-FRAME stderr lines; GpuDisplay::open_vnc
- devices DisplayBackend::Vnc; sys/linux/gpu.rs uses it instead of the window backends; the --simplefb bridge
  serves its framebuffer over VNC too; gvm_pointer_devices adds the tablet (+ mouse) whenever VNC is on
- config VncConfig: host defaults to 127.0.0.1 (DroidVM: every address), port 5900, the password from a file
  (never on the command line); validation (address literal, port >= 1024, readable password file, vnc feature)
- CREDITS entry

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
